\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Differences from the matched white-male condition for positive and negative outcomes (columns). The top row reports $\Delta _{\mathrm  {proj}}$, based on the normalized projection in Equation~\ref {eq:naturalistic-projection-normalization}; the bottom row reports $\Delta _{\mathrm  {rating}}$. Equation~\ref {eq:naturalistic-white-male-contrasts} defines both differences and their averages across models and scenarios. Appendix~\ref {app:confidence-intervals} describes the error bars. Olive and coral indicate positive and negative outcomes, respectively. Matching dashed lines give the corresponding non-demographic-baseline-minus-white-male differences, and solid gray lines mark zero. \textbf  {Positive-outcome CAA projections increase across demographic conditions, while minority women exceed white men in both negative-outcome measures.}}}{7}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:naturalistic-aggregate}{{5}{7}{Differences from the matched white-male condition for positive and negative outcomes (columns). The top row reports $\Delta _{\mathrm {proj}}$, based on the normalized projection in Equation~\ref {eq:naturalistic-projection-normalization}; the bottom row reports $\Delta _{\mathrm {rating}}$. Equation~\ref {eq:naturalistic-white-male-contrasts} defines both differences and their averages across models and scenarios. Appendix~\ref {app:confidence-intervals} describes the error bars. Olive and coral indicate positive and negative outcomes, respectively. Matching dashed lines give the corresponding non-demographic-baseline-minus-white-male differences, and solid gray lines mark zero. \textbf {Positive-outcome CAA projections increase across demographic conditions, while minority women exceed white men in both negative-outcome measures.}}{figure.caption.17}{}}
